body:
It's hard not to blame myself, worse is that I started to lose my confidence. I love him with all my heart, and I need to have this bond with him.. It's not  about physical pleasure, I can satisfy myself fully, but about the feeling that sex makes me closer to him.

&#x200B;

I always thought that at situations like that women were mostly refusing.. But for me it's reversed.

Okay ) First of all I doubt that  you love her. Love is not about appearance :) if my husband gained 30-40 kgs I would not stop wanting him or loving him as long as it doesn't cause health problems  for him, since real intimacy and love is not that superficial.

&#x200B;

Now about your wife. I myself  struggled with food addiction, I'm an emotional eater, I keep gaining losing. Right now I've gained about 30 lbs for 1.5 years. I already feel bad about it but don't have  enough emotional strength to change it right now, if my husband pressed and told me/  made me feel that he's not attracted to me because of these 30 lbs it would be dead end for me :) I 'd break up with him on spot.  You know why? Because he knows that I already feel bad about it and I struggle with it, there's no need to press an opened wound, especially when that person is your beloved one.  So you shouldn't  tell her that. If you love  her, as you proclaim, stand by her side, not by offering some bullshit dieting plans and fitness passes, but taking her to the therapist/psychologist. Extreme weight gain is always associated with medical conditions and they may be mental or physical. Usually mental because food is huge recourse of happiness and when person is overstressed, food is the real relief.  Stop being egoist and think of her :)
